  "name": "When to Make a Move",
  "slug": "when-to-make-a-move",
  "sourceLocator": {
    "chapter": "RUNNING AN ADVENTURE",
    "heading": "WHEN TO MAKE A MOVE",
    "lineStart": 4518,
    "lineEnd": 4528,
    "pdfPageStart": 86,
    "pdfPageEnd": 86
  },
  "rulesText": "The GM can make a GM move whenever you want, but the frequency and severity depends on the type of story you’re telling, the actions your players take, and the tone of the session you’re running.\n\nMake a GM move when the players:\n\n- Roll with Fear\n- Fail an action roll\n- Do something that has unavoidable consequences\n- Give you a “golden opportunity” (an opening that demands an immediate response)\n- Look to you for what happens next",
  "htmlPage": {
    "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/when-to-make-a-move/"
  },
